IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sgn-register`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), Part 11A, LAYER 1, sixth module: ss 386AM (the power to enforce), 386AN (the central register of controllers), 386ANA (the central registers
-- of nominee directors and nominee shareholders), 386AO (codes of practice) and 386AP (exemption).
--
-- These are mostly provisions addressed to the Registrar, an officer of the Authority or the Minister. They are encoded for what they decide (the Brief: no seat for an official),
-- and the seat layer asks only what they mean to the person: what may be required of the person, what the person must lodge and by when, who may see the registers, what is an offence.
--
-- GRANTS. A function named for a power ("may") answers NOTHING, not JUST FALSE, where a limit in the text's own wording is not met (the ruling of 2026-11-12, limit (1)); where the gate is "where"
-- or "when" the answer is left as the periods ruling (b) gives it, JUST FALSE, and the site is listed in the fork register for a lawyer (limit (3); fork F-AM1, F-AN1).
--
-- THE PRESCRIBED THINGS. The form, manner and time of lodgment (ss 386AN(3), 386ANA(3)), the information, persons and circumstances of disclosure (ss 386AN(6), 386ANA(6)) are inputs;
-- a prescribed time is a number of days (assumed; fork F-AF4).
--
-- READING A RESULT: see the header of sgn-application.l4.

§ `Section 386AM: power to enforce`

-- (1): the three powers.
DECLARE `s 386AM(1) paragraph` IS ONE OF
    `s 386AM(1)(a) require a company or foreign company to which this Part applies to produce its registers and documents`
    `s 386AM(1)(b) inspect, examine and make copies of the registers and any document so produced`
    `s 386AM(1)(c) make such inquiry as may be necessary to ascertain whether the provisions of this Part are complied with`

-- src:26766 | 386AM.—(1) The Registrar or an officer of the Authority may —
-- src:26768 | (a) require a company or foreign company to which this Part
-- src:26769 | applies to produce its register, its register of nominee
-- src:26770 | directors, its register of nominee shareholders and any
-- src:26775 | other document relating to those registers or the keeping of
-- src:26776 | those registers;
-- src:26780 | (b) inspect, examine and make copies of the registers and any
-- src:26781 | document so produced; and
-- src:26783 | (c) make such inquiry as may be necessary to ascertain
-- src:26784 | whether the provisions of this Part are complied with.
@ref s 386AM(1) (src:26766-26784)
GIVEN paragraph IS A `s 386AM(1) paragraph`
      `the person is the Registrar or an officer of the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a company or foreign company to which this Part applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the inquiry is necessary to ascertain whether the provisions of this Part are complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AM(1) the Registrar or an officer of the Authority may exercise the power` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person is the Registrar or an officer of the Authority`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (1) grants the powers to "The Registrar or an officer of the Authority" (a public agency's exercise is s 386AM(3))
    ELSE CONSIDER paragraph
         WHEN `s 386AM(1)(a) require a company or foreign company to which this Part applies to produce its registers and documents` THEN
             (IF `the body is a company or foreign company to which this Part applies` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (a) speaks of "a company or foreign company to which this Part applies" (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit (1))
         WHEN `s 386AM(1)(b) inspect, examine and make copies of the registers and any document so produced` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 386AM(1)(c) make such inquiry as may be necessary to ascertain whether the provisions of this Part are complied with` THEN
             (IF `the inquiry is necessary to ascertain whether the provisions of this Part are complied with` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (c) speaks of "such inquiry as may be necessary"

-- (2): where the register or documents are kept in electronic form. A power gated by "where": left as ruling (b) gives it, JUST FALSE, and listed (fork F-AM1).
DECLARE `s 386AM(2) paragraph` IS ONE OF
    `s 386AM(2)(a) require a copy of the register or documents to be made available in legible form`
    `s 386AM(2)(b) require any person on the premises to give such assistance as the Registrar or officer may reasonably require`

-- src:26788 | (2) Where any register or documents as are mentioned in
-- src:26789 | subsection (1) are kept in electronic form —
-- src:26791 | (a) the power of the Registrar or an officer of the Authority in
-- src:26792 | subsection (1)(a) to require the register or any documents
-- src:26793 | to be produced includes the power to require a copy of the
-- src:26794 | register or documents to be made available in legible form
-- src:26795 | and subsection (1)(b) is to accordingly apply in relation to
-- src:26796 | any copy so made available; and
-- src:26798 | (b) the power of the Registrar or an officer of the Authority
-- src:26799 | under subsection (1)(b) to inspect the register or any
-- src:26800 | documents includes the power to require any person on the
-- src:26801 | premises in question to give the Registrar or the officer of
-- src:26802 | the Authority such assistance as the Registrar or officer
-- src:26803 | may reasonably require to enable the Registrar or officer to
-- src:26804 | inspect and make copies of the register or documents in
-- src:26805 | legible form, and to make records of the information
-- src:26806 | contained in them.
@ref s 386AM(2) (src:26788-26806)
GIVEN paragraph IS A `s 386AM(2) paragraph`
      `the register or documents mentioned in subsection (1) are kept in electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AM(2) the power of the Registrar or an officer of the Authority extends to the requirement` MEANS
    IF `the register or documents mentioned in subsection (1) are kept in electronic form`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); listed for a lawyer, fork F-AM1 and the grant ruling's limit (3)): "Where any register or documents as are mentioned in subsection (1) are kept in electronic form"

-- (3): a public agency may exercise the powers, to enable it to administer or enforce a written law.
-- src:26810 | (3) The powers conferred on the Registrar or an officer of the
-- src:26811 | Authority under subsections (1) and (2) may be exercised by a public
-- src:26812 | agency to enable the public agency to administer or enforce any
-- src:26813 | written law.
@ref s 386AM(3) (src:26810-26813)
GIVEN `the person is a public agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exercise is to enable the public agency to administer or enforce a written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AM(3) the public agency may exercise the powers conferred by subsections (1) and (2)` MEANS
    IF `the person is a public agency` AND `the exercise is to enable the public agency to administer or enforce a written law`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be exercised by a public agency to enable the public agency to administer or enforce any written law"

-- (4): the offence of failing to comply with a requirement under (1) or (2).
-- src:26817 | (4) Any person who fails to comply with any requirement imposed
-- src:26818 | under subsection (1) or (2) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be
-- src:26819 | liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $25,000.
@ref s 386AM(4) (src:26817-26819)
GIVEN `the person fails to comply with a requirement imposed under subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AM(4) the person is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF `the person fails to comply with a requirement imposed under subsection (1) or (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question; split site (i)): "Any person who fails to comply with any requirement imposed under subsection (1) or (2) shall be guilty of an offence"

-- src:26817 | (4) Any person who fails to comply with any requirement imposed
-- src:26818 | under subsection (1) or (2) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be
-- src:26819 | liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $25,000.
@ref s 386AM(4) (src:26817-26819)
GIVEN `the person fails to comply with a requirement imposed under subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 386AM(4) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 386AM(4) the person is guilty of the offence` `the person fails to comply with a requirement imposed under subsection (1) or (2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 25000, 0, FALSE, FALSE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

-- (4A): the offence of providing false or misleading information.
-- src:26828 | (4A) A person who, in complying with a requirement imposed, or
-- src:26829 | in answering an inquiry made, under subsection (1) or (2), provides
-- src:26830 | any information that is false or misleading in a material particular to
-- src:26831 | the Registrar or an officer of the Authority, shall be guilty of an
-- src:26832 | offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:26833 | $25,000.
@ref s 386AM(4A) (src:26828-26833)
GIVEN `the person, in complying with a requirement imposed, or in answering an inquiry made, under subsection (1) or (2), provides to the Registrar or an officer of the Authority information that is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AM(4A) the person is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF `the person, in complying with a requirement imposed, or in answering an inquiry made, under subsection (1) or (2), provides to the Registrar or an officer of the Authority information that is false or misleading in a material particular`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question; split site (i)): "A person who, in complying with a requirement imposed, or in answering an inquiry made, under subsection (1) or (2), provides any information that is false or misleading in a material particular to the Registrar or an officer of the Authority, shall be guilty of an offence"

-- src:26828 | (4A) A person who, in complying with a requirement imposed, or
-- src:26829 | in answering an inquiry made, under subsection (1) or (2), provides
-- src:26830 | any information that is false or misleading in a material particular to
-- src:26831 | the Registrar or an officer of the Authority, shall be guilty of an
-- src:26832 | offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:26833 | $25,000.
@ref s 386AM(4A) (src:26828-26833)
GIVEN `the person, in complying with a requirement imposed, or in answering an inquiry made, under subsection (1) or (2), provides to the Registrar or an officer of the Authority information that is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 386AM(4A) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 386AM(4A) the person is guilty of the offence` `the person, in complying with a requirement imposed, or in answering an inquiry made, under subsection (1) or (2), provides to the Registrar or an officer of the Authority information that is false or misleading in a material particular` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 25000, 0, FALSE, FALSE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

-- (4B): the defence ("it is a defence ... to prove"): where it is not proved the answer is JUST FALSE, worded "this section gives no defence on these facts" (the ruling of 2026-11-05 on defences, item (b)).
-- src:26837 | (4B) In proceedings for an offence under subsection (4A), it is a
-- src:26838 | defence to the charge for the accused to prove, on a balance of
-- src:26839 | probabilities, that the accused took all reasonable steps and exercised
-- src:26840 | all due diligence to ensure that the information provided was not false
-- src:26841 | or misleading.
@ref s 386AM(4B) (src:26837-26841)
GIVEN `the proceedings are for an offence under subsection (4A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused has proved, on a balance of probabilities, that the accused took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to ensure that the information provided was not false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AM(4B) this section gives a defence on these facts` MEANS
    IF NOT `the proceedings are for an offence under subsection (4A)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (4B) speaks of "proceedings for an offence under subsection (4A)"
    ELSE (IF `the accused has proved, on a balance of probabilities, that the accused took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to ensure that the information provided was not false or misleading`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the ruling of 2026-11-05 on defences, item (b)): "it is a defence to the charge for the accused to prove, on a balance of probabilities, that the accused took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence"; read as "this section gives no defence on these facts", never "no defence at all"

-- (5): in addition to the right of inspection under s 396A (a rule with one answer).
-- src:26845 | (5) This section applies in addition to any right of inspection
-- src:26846 | conferred by section 396A.
@ref s 386AM(5) (src:26845-26846)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 386AM(5) this section applies in addition to any right of inspection conferred by section 396A` MEANS TRUE

-- (6): "public agency".
-- src:26850 | (6) In this section, “public agency” means a public officer, an Organ
-- src:26851 | of State or a ministry or department of the Government, or a public
-- src:26852 | authority established by or under any public Act for a public purpose
-- src:26853 | or a member, an officer or an employee, or any department, thereof.
@ref s 386AM(6) (src:26850-26853)
GIVEN `the person is a public officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an Organ of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a ministry or department of the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a public authority established by or under a public Act for a public purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member, officer or employee, or a department, of a public authority so established` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AM(6) "public agency" the person is a public agency` MEANS
    IF    `the person is a public officer`
       OR `the person is an Organ of State`
       OR `the person is a ministry or department of the Government`
       OR `the person is a public authority established by or under a public Act for a public purpose`
       OR `the person is a member, officer or employee, or a department, of a public authority so established`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“public agency” means a public officer, an Organ of State or a ministry or department of the Government, or a public authority ..." ("means": a closed definition; "public officer" and "Organ of State" are taken as inputs, being defined elsewhere)

§ `Section 386AN: the central register of controllers`

-- (1) and (2): this section applies where the Minister, by notification in the Gazette, directs the Registrar to maintain a central register.
-- src:26859 | 386AN.—(1) This section applies where the Minister, by
-- src:26860 | notification in the Gazette, directs the Registrar to maintain a
-- src:26861 | central register of controllers of companies and foreign companies.
@ref s 386AN(1) (src:26859-26861)
GIVEN `the Minister has, by notification in the Gazette, directed the Registrar to maintain a central register of controllers of companies and foreign companies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AN(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF `the Minister has, by notification in the Gazette, directed the Registrar to maintain a central register of controllers of companies and foreign companies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)): "This section applies where the Minister, by notification in the Gazette, directs the Registrar to maintain a central register of controllers"

-- src:26865 | (2) Where the Minister has directed the Registrar to maintain a
-- src:26866 | central register of controllers of companies and foreign companies
-- src:26867 | under subsection (1) —
-- src:26869 | (a) the Registrar must keep a central register of controllers
-- src:26870 | consisting of the particulars contained in the registers kept
-- src:26871 | by companies and foreign companies to which this Part
-- src:26872 | applies; and
@ref s 386AN(2) (src:26865-26872)
GIVEN `the Minister has directed the Registrar to maintain a central register of controllers of companies and foreign companies under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AN(2) the duties of paragraphs (a) and (b) apply to the Registrar` MEANS
    IF `the Minister has directed the Registrar to maintain a central register of controllers of companies and foreign companies under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)): "Where the Minister has directed the Registrar to maintain a central register ... under subsection (1) — (a) the Registrar must keep ...; and (b) the Registrar must require ..."

-- src:26869 | (a) the Registrar must keep a central register of controllers
-- src:26870 | consisting of the particulars contained in the registers kept
-- src:26871 | by companies and foreign companies to which this Part
-- src:26872 | applies; and
@ref s 386AN(2)(a) (src:26869-26872)
GIVEN `the Registrar` IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 386AN act`
`s 386AN(2)(a) the Registrar must keep a central register of controllers` MEANS
    PARTY `the Registrar`
    MUST `s 386AN(2)(a) keep a central register of controllers consisting of the particulars contained in the registers kept by companies and foreign companies to which this Part applies`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 386AN(2)(a) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY `the Registrar` BECAUSE "the Registrar did not keep the central register of controllers (s 386AN(2)(a))" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: maintenance; see notes]

-- src:26874 | (b) the Registrar must require any company or foreign
-- src:26875 | company to which this Part applies to lodge with the
-- src:26876 | Registrar —
-- src:26881 | (i) all particulars contained in the company’s or foreign
-- src:26882 | company’s register maintained under section 386AF
-- src:26883 | (including the matters mentioned in
-- src:26884 | section 386AFA(3)); and
-- src:26888 | (ii) all updates to the company’s or foreign company’s
-- src:26889 | register that occur after the lodgment of the
-- src:26890 | particulars under sub‑paragraph (i).
@ref s 386AN(2)(b) (src:26874-26890)
GIVEN `the Registrar` IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 386AN act`
`s 386AN(2)(b) the Registrar must require each company or foreign company to lodge the particulars and updates` MEANS
    PARTY `the Registrar`
    MUST `s 386AN(2)(b) require a company or foreign company to which this Part applies to lodge the particulars contained in its register and all later updates`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 386AN(2)(b) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY `the Registrar` BECAUSE "the Registrar did not require the company or foreign company to lodge the particulars and updates (s 386AN(2)(b))" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- (3): the company must lodge in the prescribed form and manner, within the prescribed time, after the Registrar requires.
-- src:26894 | (3) Where the Registrar requires a company or foreign company to
-- src:26895 | lodge with the Registrar the particulars, matters and updates
-- src:26896 | mentioned in subsection (2)(b), the company or foreign company
-- src:26897 | must lodge the particulars, matters and updates in the prescribed form
-- src:26898 | and manner and within the prescribed time.
@ref s 386AN(3) (src:26894-26898)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company has lodged the particulars, matters and updates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the lodgment is in the prescribed form and manner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the company or foreign company lodged them` IS A DATE
      `the day the Registrar required the company or foreign company to lodge them` IS A DATE
      `the prescribed time, in days` IS A NUMBER
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AN(3) the company or foreign company has lodged what the Registrar required in time and in the prescribed form and manner` MEANS
    `s 386AF(8) timing: the act was done in time` (`the company or foreign company has lodged the particulars, matters and updates` AND `the lodgment is in the prescribed form and manner`) `the day the company or foreign company lodged them` `the day the Registrar required the company or foreign company to lodge them` `the prescribed time, in days` `the date asked`   -- FALSE-kind where late or not in the prescribed form and manner ("must lodge ... in the prescribed form and manner and within the prescribed time": a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a)); NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) while the time has not run out

-- src:26894 | (3) Where the Registrar requires a company or foreign company to
-- src:26895 | lodge with the Registrar the particulars, matters and updates
-- src:26896 | mentioned in subsection (2)(b), the company or foreign company
-- src:26897 | must lodge the particulars, matters and updates in the prescribed form
-- src:26898 | and manner and within the prescribed time.
@ref s 386AN(3) (src:26894-26898)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company` IS A Party
      `the prescribed time, in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 386AN act`
`s 386AN(3) a company or foreign company must lodge the particulars, matters and updates within the prescribed time after the Registrar requires it` MEANS
    PARTY `the company or foreign company`
    MUST `s 386AN(3) lodge with the Registrar the particulars, matters and updates in the prescribed form and manner`
    WITHIN `the prescribed time, in days`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the company or foreign company` BECAUSE "the company did not lodge the particulars, matters and updates within the prescribed time after the Registrar required it (s 386AN(3), (4))"

-- (4): the offence.
-- src:26902 | (4) If a company or foreign company fails to comply with
-- src:26903 | subsection (3), the company or foreign company, and every officer
-- src:26904 | of the company or foreign company who is in default, shall each be
-- src:26905 | guilty of an offence and shall each be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:26906 | exceeding $25,000.
@ref s 386AN(4) (src:26902-26906)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company fails to comply with subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AN(4) the company or foreign company is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF `the company or foreign company fails to comply with subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question; split site (i)): "shall each be guilty of an offence and shall each be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $25,000"

-- src:26902 | (4) If a company or foreign company fails to comply with
-- src:26903 | subsection (3), the company or foreign company, and every officer
-- src:26904 | of the company or foreign company who is in default, shall each be
-- src:26905 | guilty of an offence and shall each be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:26906 | exceeding $25,000.
@ref s 386AN(4) (src:26902-26906)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company fails to comply with subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company or foreign company who is in default, as section 408(3) gives that meaning` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AN(4) the officer of the company or foreign company is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF `the company or foreign company fails to comply with subsection (3)` AND `the person is an officer of the company or foreign company who is in default, as section 408(3) gives that meaning`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question; split site (i)): "and every officer of the company or foreign company who is in default, shall each be guilty of an offence"

-- src:26902 | (4) If a company or foreign company fails to comply with
-- src:26903 | subsection (3), the company or foreign company, and every officer
-- src:26904 | of the company or foreign company who is in default, shall each be
-- src:26905 | guilty of an offence and shall each be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:26906 | exceeding $25,000.
@ref s 386AN(4) (src:26902-26906)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company fails to comply with subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company or foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company or foreign company who is in default, as section 408(3) gives that meaning` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 386AN(4) the most the company or foreign company or an officer in default may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF (IF `the person is the company or foreign company`
        THEN `s 386AN(4) the company or foreign company is guilty of the offence` `the company or foreign company fails to comply with subsection (3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        ELSE `s 386AN(4) the officer of the company or foreign company is guilty of the offence` `the company or foreign company fails to comply with subsection (3)` `the person is an officer of the company or foreign company who is in default, as section 408(3) gives that meaning` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 25000, 0, FALSE, FALSE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

-- (5) and (6): the Registrar must not disclose the central register to a member of the public, subject to (6).
-- src:26914 | (5) Subject to subsection (6), the Registrar must not disclose, or
-- src:26915 | make available for inspection, the central register of controllers of
-- src:26916 | companies and foreign companies kept by the Registrar under this
-- src:26917 | section to any member of the public.
@ref s 386AN(5) (src:26914-26917)
GIVEN `the person is a member of the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is one that subsection (6) allows` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AN(5) the Registrar is barred from disclosing the central register to the person` MEANS
    IF `the disclosure is one that subsection (6) allows`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subsection (6), the Registrar must not disclose ..." read as: where the disclosure is one subsection (6) allows the bar does not apply
    ELSE (IF `the person is a member of the public`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on disclosure "to any member of the public"

-- src:26914 | (5) Subject to subsection (6), the Registrar must not disclose, or
-- src:26915 | make available for inspection, the central register of controllers of
-- src:26916 | companies and foreign companies kept by the Registrar under this
-- src:26917 | section to any member of the public.
@ref s 386AN(5) (src:26914-26917)
GIVEN `the Registrar` IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 386AN act`
`s 386AN(5) the Registrar must not disclose the central register of controllers to a member of the public` MEANS
    PARTY `the Registrar`
    SHANT `s 386AN(5) disclose the central register of controllers, or make it available for inspection, to a member of the public`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Registrar` BECAUSE "the Registrar disclosed the central register of controllers, or made it available for inspection, to a member of the public (s 386AN(5))"

-- src:26921 | (6) The Registrar may disclose prescribed information in the central
-- src:26922 | register of controllers of companies and foreign companies to
-- src:26923 | prescribed persons under prescribed circumstances.
@ref s 386AN(6) (src:26921-26923)
GIVEN `the information is prescribed information in the central register of controllers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a prescribed person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circumstances are prescribed circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AN(6) the Registrar may disclose the information to the person` MEANS
    IF `the information is prescribed information in the central register of controllers` AND `the person is a prescribed person` AND `the circumstances are prescribed circumstances`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text, and limited by its own wording): "may disclose prescribed information ... to prescribed persons under prescribed circumstances"; the regulations are not a source

-- src:26927 | (7) To avoid doubt, different information and persons may be
-- src:26928 | prescribed under subsection (6) for different prescribed
-- src:26929 | circumstances.
@ref s 386AN(7) (src:26927-26929)
GIVEN `the circumstances differ from those for which the information and persons were prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AN(7) different information and persons may be prescribed for the different circumstances` MEANS
    IF `the circumstances differ from those for which the information and persons were prescribed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (7) says only that different information and persons "may be prescribed ... for different prescribed circumstances"

DECLARE `s 386AN act` IS ONE OF
    `s 386AN(2)(a) keep a central register of controllers consisting of the particulars contained in the registers kept by companies and foreign companies to which this Part applies`
    `s 386AN(2)(b) require a company or foreign company to which this Part applies to lodge the particulars contained in its register and all later updates`
    `s 386AN(3) lodge with the Registrar the particulars, matters and updates in the prescribed form and manner`
    `s 386AN(5) disclose the central register of controllers, or make it available for inspection, to a member of the public`

§ `Section 386ANA: the central registers of nominee directors and nominee shareholders`

-- src:26939 | 386ANA.—(1) The Registrar must keep a central register of
-- src:26940 | nominee directors and a central register of nominee shareholders
-- src:26941 | consisting of the particulars contained in the registers kept by
-- src:26942 | companies and foreign companies to which this Part applies.
@ref s 386ANA(1) (src:26939-26942)
GIVEN `the Registrar` IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 386ANA act`
`s 386ANA(1) the Registrar must keep a central register of nominee directors and a central register of nominee shareholders` MEANS
    PARTY `the Registrar`
    MUST `s 386ANA(1) keep a central register of nominee directors and a central register of nominee shareholders`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 386ANA(1) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY `the Registrar` BECAUSE "the Registrar did not keep the central registers of nominee directors and nominee shareholders (s 386ANA(1))" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: maintenance; see notes]

-- (2): what the company must lodge: the four items.
-- src:26944 | (2) A company or foreign company to which this Part applies must
-- src:26945 | lodge with the Registrar —
-- src:26947 | (a) all particulars contained in the company’s or foreign
-- src:26948 | company’s register of nominee directors maintained under
-- src:26949 | section 386AKA;
-- src:26951 | (b) all updates to that register that occur after the lodgment of
-- src:26952 | the particulars under paragraph (a);
-- src:26954 | (c) all particulars contained in the company’s or foreign
-- src:26955 | company’s register of nominee shareholders maintained
-- src:26956 | under section 386ALA; and
-- src:26958 | (d) all updates to that register that occur after the lodgment of
-- src:26959 | the particulars under paragraph (c).
@ref s 386ANA(2) (src:26944-26959)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company has lodged all particulars contained in its register of nominee directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company or foreign company has lodged all updates to that register that occurred after the lodgment of the particulars` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company or foreign company has lodged all particulars contained in its register of nominee shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company or foreign company has lodged all updates to that register that occurred after the lodgment of the particulars of nominee shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386ANA(2) the company or foreign company has lodged what the subsection requires` MEANS
    JUST (   `the company or foreign company has lodged all particulars contained in its register of nominee directors`
         AND `the company or foreign company has lodged all updates to that register that occurred after the lodgment of the particulars`
         AND `the company or foreign company has lodged all particulars contained in its register of nominee shareholders`
         AND `the company or foreign company has lodged all updates to that register that occurred after the lodgment of the particulars of nominee shareholders`)   -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question): "must lodge with the Registrar — (a) ...; (b) ...; (c) ...; and (d) ..."

-- src:26961 | (3) The company or foreign company must lodge the particulars,
-- src:26962 | matters and updates in the prescribed form and manner and within the
-- src:26963 | prescribed time.
@ref s 386ANA(3) (src:26961-26963)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company has lodged the particulars, matters and updates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the lodgment is in the prescribed form and manner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the company or foreign company lodged them` IS A DATE
      `the day the prescribed time began to run` IS A DATE
      `the prescribed time, in days` IS A NUMBER
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386ANA(3) the company or foreign company has lodged in time and in the prescribed form and manner` MEANS
    `s 386AF(8) timing: the act was done in time` (`the company or foreign company has lodged the particulars, matters and updates` AND `the lodgment is in the prescribed form and manner`) `the day the company or foreign company lodged them` `the day the prescribed time began to run` `the prescribed time, in days` `the date asked`   -- FALSE-kind where late or not in the prescribed form and manner ("must lodge ... in the prescribed form and manner and within the prescribed time": ruling (a)); NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) while the time has not run out. The day the prescribed time begins is not stated by the subsection: an input (fork F-ANA1)

-- src:26961 | (3) The company or foreign company must lodge the particulars,
-- src:26962 | matters and updates in the prescribed form and manner and within the
-- src:26963 | prescribed time.
@ref s 386ANA(3) (src:26961-26963)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company` IS A Party
      `the prescribed time, in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 386ANA act`
`s 386ANA(3) a company or foreign company must lodge the particulars, matters and updates within the prescribed time` MEANS
    PARTY `the company or foreign company`
    MUST `s 386ANA(3) lodge with the Registrar the particulars and updates of its registers of nominee directors and nominee shareholders in the prescribed form and manner`
    WITHIN `the prescribed time, in days`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the company or foreign company` BECAUSE "the company did not lodge the particulars and updates of its registers of nominee directors and nominee shareholders within the prescribed time (s 386ANA(2), (3), (4))"

-- src:26965 | (4) If a company or foreign company fails to comply with
-- src:26966 | subsection (2) or (3), the company or foreign company, and every
-- src:26967 | officer of the company or foreign company who is in default, shall
-- src:26968 | each be guilty of an offence and shall each be liable on conviction to a
-- src:26969 | fine not exceeding $25,000.
@ref s 386ANA(4) (src:26965-26969)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company fails to comply with subsection (2) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386ANA(4) the company or foreign company is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF `the company or foreign company fails to comply with subsection (2) or (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question; split site (i)): "shall each be guilty of an offence and shall each be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $25,000"

-- src:26965 | (4) If a company or foreign company fails to comply with
-- src:26966 | subsection (2) or (3), the company or foreign company, and every
-- src:26967 | officer of the company or foreign company who is in default, shall
-- src:26968 | each be guilty of an offence and shall each be liable on conviction to a
-- src:26969 | fine not exceeding $25,000.
@ref s 386ANA(4) (src:26965-26969)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company fails to comply with subsection (2) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company or foreign company who is in default, as section 408(3) gives that meaning` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386ANA(4) the officer of the company or foreign company is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF `the company or foreign company fails to comply with subsection (2) or (3)` AND `the person is an officer of the company or foreign company who is in default, as section 408(3) gives that meaning`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question; split site (i)): "and every officer of the company or foreign company who is in default, shall each be guilty of an offence"

-- src:26965 | (4) If a company or foreign company fails to comply with
-- src:26966 | subsection (2) or (3), the company or foreign company, and every
-- src:26967 | officer of the company or foreign company who is in default, shall
-- src:26968 | each be guilty of an offence and shall each be liable on conviction to a
-- src:26969 | fine not exceeding $25,000.
@ref s 386ANA(4) (src:26965-26969)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company fails to comply with subsection (2) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company or foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company or foreign company who is in default, as section 408(3) gives that meaning` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 386ANA(4) the most the company or foreign company or an officer in default may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF (IF `the person is the company or foreign company`
        THEN `s 386ANA(4) the company or foreign company is guilty of the offence` `the company or foreign company fails to comply with subsection (2) or (3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        ELSE `s 386ANA(4) the officer of the company or foreign company is guilty of the offence` `the company or foreign company fails to comply with subsection (2) or (3)` `the person is an officer of the company or foreign company who is in default, as section 408(3) gives that meaning` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 25000, 0, FALSE, FALSE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

-- src:26971 | (5) Subject to subsection (6), the Registrar must not disclose, or
-- src:26972 | make available for inspection, the central register of nominee
-- src:26973 | directors or the central register of nominee shareholders kept by
-- src:26974 | the Registrar under this section to any member of the public.
@ref s 386ANA(5) (src:26971-26974)
GIVEN `the person is a member of the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is one that subsection (6) allows` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386ANA(5) the Registrar is barred from disclosing the central registers of nominee directors and nominee shareholders to the person` MEANS
    IF `the disclosure is one that subsection (6) allows`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subsection (6), the Registrar must not disclose ..." read as: where the disclosure is one subsection (6) allows the bar does not apply
    ELSE (IF `the person is a member of the public`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on disclosure "to any member of the public"

-- src:26971 | (5) Subject to subsection (6), the Registrar must not disclose, or
-- src:26972 | make available for inspection, the central register of nominee
-- src:26973 | directors or the central register of nominee shareholders kept by
-- src:26974 | the Registrar under this section to any member of the public.
@ref s 386ANA(5) (src:26971-26974)
GIVEN `the Registrar` IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 386ANA act`
`s 386ANA(5) the Registrar must not disclose the central registers of nominee directors and nominee shareholders to a member of the public` MEANS
    PARTY `the Registrar`
    SHANT `s 386ANA(5) disclose the central register of nominee directors or the central register of nominee shareholders, or make it available for inspection, to a member of the public`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Registrar` BECAUSE "the Registrar disclosed a central register of nominee directors or nominee shareholders, or made it available for inspection, to a member of the public (s 386ANA(5))"

-- src:26976 | (6) The Registrar may disclose prescribed information in the central
-- src:26977 | register of nominee directors or the central register of nominee
-- src:26978 | shareholders to prescribed persons under prescribed circumstances.
@ref s 386ANA(6) (src:26976-26978)
GIVEN `the information is prescribed information in the central register of nominee directors or the central register of nominee shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a prescribed person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circumstances are prescribed circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386ANA(6) the Registrar may disclose the information to the person` MEANS
    IF `the information is prescribed information in the central register of nominee directors or the central register of nominee shareholders` AND `the person is a prescribed person` AND `the circumstances are prescribed circumstances`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text, and limited by its own wording): "may disclose prescribed information ... to prescribed persons under prescribed circumstances"; the regulations are not a source

-- src:26983 | (7) To avoid doubt, different information and persons may be
-- src:26984 | prescribed under subsection (6) for different prescribed
-- src:26985 | circumstances.
@ref s 386ANA(7) (src:26983-26985)
GIVEN `the circumstances differ from those for which the information and persons were prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386ANA(7) different information and persons may be prescribed for the different circumstances` MEANS
    IF `the circumstances differ from those for which the information and persons were prescribed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (7) says only that different information and persons "may be prescribed ... for different prescribed circumstances"

DECLARE `s 386ANA act` IS ONE OF
    `s 386ANA(1) keep a central register of nominee directors and a central register of nominee shareholders`
    `s 386ANA(3) lodge with the Registrar the particulars and updates of its registers of nominee directors and nominee shareholders in the prescribed form and manner`
    `s 386ANA(5) disclose the central register of nominee directors or the central register of nominee shareholders, or make it available for inspection, to a member of the public`

§ `Section 386AO: codes of practice`

-- (1): the Registrar may issue the instruments, for either purpose.
DECLARE `s 386AO instrument` IS ONE OF
    `s 386AO a code`
    `s 386AO guidance`
    `s 386AO a guideline`
    `s 386AO a policy statement`
    `s 386AO a practice direction`
    `s 386AO some other instrument`

-- src:26991 | 386AO.—(1) The Registrar may issue one or more codes,
-- src:26992 | guidance, guidelines, policy statements and practice directions for
-- src:26993 | all or any of the following purposes:
-- src:26995 | (a) to provide guidance to companies or foreign companies, or
-- src:26996 | to both, in relation to the operation or administration of any
-- src:26997 | provision of this Part;
-- src:26999 | (b) generally for carrying out the purposes of this Part.
@ref s 386AO(1) (src:26991-26999)
GIVEN `the instrument` IS A `s 386AO instrument`
      `the purpose is to provide guidance to companies or foreign companies, or to both, in relation to the operation or administration of a provision of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is generally to carry out the purposes of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AO(1) the Registrar may issue the instrument for the purpose` MEANS
    IF    `the instrument` EQUALS `s 386AO some other instrument`
       OR ((NOT `the purpose is to provide guidance to companies or foreign companies, or to both, in relation to the operation or administration of a provision of this Part`) AND (NOT `the purpose is generally to carry out the purposes of this Part`))
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (1) lists "codes, guidance, guidelines, policy statements and practice directions" and the purposes in paragraphs (a) and (b); another instrument or purpose is outside the limit (the grant ruling, limit (1))
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:27003 | (2) The Registrar may publish any such code, guidance, guideline,
-- src:27004 | policy statement or practice direction, in such manner as the Registrar
-- src:27005 | thinks fit.
@ref s 386AO(2) (src:27003-27005)
GIVEN `the instrument has been issued under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AO(2) the Registrar may publish the instrument in such manner as the Registrar thinks fit` MEANS
    IF `the instrument has been issued under this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (2) speaks of "any such code, guidance, guideline, policy statement or practice direction"

-- src:27009 | (3) The Registrar may revoke, vary, revise or amend the whole or
-- src:27010 | any part of any code, guidance, guideline, policy statement or practice
-- src:27011 | direction issued under this section in such manner as the Registrar
-- src:27012 | thinks fit.
@ref s 386AO(3) (src:27009-27012)
GIVEN `the instrument has been issued under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AO(3) the Registrar may revoke, vary, revise or amend the instrument` MEANS
    IF `the instrument has been issued under this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (3) speaks of an instrument "issued under this section"

-- (4)(b): a reference to the instrument is a reference to it as amended, "unless the context otherwise requires".
-- src:27016 | (4) Where amendments are made under subsection (3) —
-- src:27018 | (a) the other provisions of this section apply, with the
-- src:27019 | necessary modifications, to such amendments as they
-- src:27020 | apply to the code, guidance, guideline, policy statement
-- src:27021 | and practice direction; and
-- src:27023 | (b) any reference in this Act or any other written law to the
-- src:27024 | code, guidance, guideline, policy statement or practice
-- src:27025 | direction however expressed is to be treated, unless the
-- src:27026 | context otherwise requires, as a reference to the code,
-- src:27027 | guidance, guideline, policy statement or practice direction
-- src:27028 | as so amended.
@ref s 386AO(4) (src:27016-27028)
GIVEN `the instrument has been amended under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AO(4)(b) a reference to the instrument is a reference to the instrument as amended` MEANS
    IF NOT `the instrument has been amended under subsection (3)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (b) speaks of amendments "made under subsection (3)"
    ELSE (IF `the context otherwise requires`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the context otherwise requires"
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- (5): failure to comply with an instrument is not of itself a criminal liability, but may be relied on.
-- src:27035 | (5) The failure by any person to comply with any of the provisions
-- src:27036 | of a code, guidance, guideline, policy statement or practice direction
-- src:27037 | issued under this section that applies to that person does not of itself
-- src:27038 | render that person liable to criminal proceedings but any such failure
-- src:27039 | may, in any proceedings whether civil or criminal, be relied upon by
-- src:27040 | any party to the proceedings as tending to establish or to negate any
-- src:27041 | liability which is in question in the proceedings.
@ref s 386AO(5) (src:27035-27041)
GIVEN `the person has failed to comply with a provision of an instrument issued under this section that applies to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AO(5) the failure of itself renders the person liable to criminal proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the person has failed to comply with a provision of an instrument issued under this section that applies to the person`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not of itself render that person liable to criminal proceedings"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (5) speaks of "The failure by any person to comply with any of the provisions of a code ... that applies to that person"

-- src:27035 | (5) The failure by any person to comply with any of the provisions
-- src:27036 | of a code, guidance, guideline, policy statement or practice direction
-- src:27037 | issued under this section that applies to that person does not of itself
-- src:27038 | render that person liable to criminal proceedings but any such failure
-- src:27039 | may, in any proceedings whether civil or criminal, be relied upon by
-- src:27040 | any party to the proceedings as tending to establish or to negate any
-- src:27041 | liability which is in question in the proceedings.
@ref s 386AO(5) (src:27035-27041)
GIVEN `the person has failed to comply with a provision of an instrument issued under this section that applies to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AO(5) a party to proceedings may rely on the failure as tending to establish or to negate a liability in question` MEANS
    IF `the person has failed to comply with a provision of an instrument issued under this section that applies to the person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the failure "may, in any proceedings whether civil or criminal, be relied upon by any party"; without the failure the subsection is silent

-- (6): the instrument may be of general or specific application and may provide for different cases.
-- src:27045 | (6) Any code, guidance, guideline, policy statement or practice
-- src:27046 | direction issued under this section —
-- src:27048 | (a) may be of general or specific application; and
-- src:27050 | (b) may specify that different provisions apply to different
-- src:27051 | circumstances or provide for different cases or classes of
-- src:27052 | cases.
@ref s 386AO(6) (src:27045-27052)
GIVEN `the instrument is of general application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is of specific application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument specifies that different provisions apply to different circumstances, or provides for different cases or classes of cases` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AO(6) the instrument is of a kind that the subsection allows` MEANS
    IF    `the instrument is of general application`
       OR `the instrument is of specific application`
       OR `the instrument specifies that different provisions apply to different circumstances, or provides for different cases or classes of cases`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may be of general or specific application" and "may specify that different provisions apply" are permissions, not a closed list

-- (7): it is not necessary to publish the instrument in the Gazette.
-- src:27056 | (7) It is not necessary to publish any code, guidance, guideline,
-- src:27057 | policy statement or practice direction issued under this section in the
-- src:27058 | Gazette.
@ref s 386AO(7) (src:27056-27058)
GIVEN `the instrument has been issued under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AO(7) the instrument must be published in the Gazette` MEANS
    IF `the instrument has been issued under this section`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is not necessary to publish any code, guidance, guideline, policy statement or practice direction issued under this section in the Gazette"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (7) speaks of an instrument "issued under this section"

§ `Section 386AP: exemption`

-- src:27064 | 386AP. The Minister may, by order in the Gazette, exempt any
-- src:27065 | person or class of persons from all or any of the provisions of this
-- src:27066 | Part.
@ref s 386AP (src:27064-27066)
GIVEN `the Minister has by order in the Gazette exempted the person, or a class of persons to which the person belongs, from the provision of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AP the person is exempt from the provision of this Part` MEANS
    IF `the Minister has by order in the Gazette exempted the person, or a class of persons to which the person belongs, from the provision of this Part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Minister may, by order in the Gazette, exempt any person or class of persons from all or any of the provisions of this Part"; without such an order the section is silent (a grant, so NOTHING and not JUST FALSE)
